msullivan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msullivan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msullivan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msullivan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-01-08T23:12:09Z","updated_at":"2020-01-08T23:12:09Z","body":"This does look like a bug, yeah. I think the issue is that when doing indexing on a type variable with a typeddict bound, checks it just as a call to `__getitem__` and ends up operating on the typeddict's \"fallback\" type, which is `typing._TypedDict`, which inherits from `Mapping[str, object]`.\r\n\r\nI think it should be pretty easy to make `visit_index_with_type` in `checkexpr.py` try recursively indexing into its bound, if you want to take a shot at fixing it.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/572302833/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"msullivan","id":340349,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0MDM0OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/340349?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/msullivan","html_url":"https://github.com/msullivan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msullivan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msullivan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msullivan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msullivan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msullivan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msullivan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msullivan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msullivan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msullivan/received_e